{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011jcMpXYCRMMycFYXkVvQcs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd040-printenv\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/printenv: Print Environment Variables\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Scripts and debugging sessions need a simple way to inspect specific environment variables\n6\t  or dump the entire environment. While env overlaps in functionality, printenv provides a\n7\t  cleaner interface for querying named variables and reporting which ones are missing via its\n8\t  exit code. The macOS BSD printenv lacks the -0 NUL-delimited flag available in GNU printenv.\n9\t  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gprintenv, installed by\n10\t  coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations and edge cases, verified by differential\n11\t  testing via pkg/testutils.\n12\t\n13\tgoals:\n14\t  - G1: Print all environment variables when invoked with no arguments.\n15\t  - G2: Print only the values of specified variables when one or more VARIABLE arguments are given.\n16\t  - G3: Report success or failure via exit code depending on whether all requested variables exist.\n17\t\n18\trequirements:\n19\t  R1:\n20\t    title: Default behavior\n21\t    items:\n22\t      - R1.1:\n23\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print every environment variable on its own line in NAME=VALUE format and exit 0.\n24\t      - R1.2:\n25\t          text: When invoked with one or more VARIABLE arguments, must print only the value (not the name or '=') of each named variable, one per line, in the order given.\n26\t      - R1.3:\n27\t          text: If a named VARIABLE is not set in the environment, must produce no output for that variable and must not print an error message.\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Output formatting and exit codes\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: -0 or --null must terminate each output line with a NUL byte (0x00) instead of a newline.\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: Must exit 0 if all requested VARIABLE arguments are found in the environment.\n36\t      - R2.3:\n37\t          text: Must exit 1 if any requested VARIABLE argument is not found in the environment.\n38\t      - R2.4:\n39\t          text: When no VARIABLE arguments are given, must always exit 0 (the dump of all variables cannot fail).\n40\t\n41\t  R3:\n42\t    title: Differential testing\n43\t    items:\n44\t      - R3.1:\n45\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (gprintenv) via pkg/testutils.\n46\t      - R3.2:\n47\t          text: \"Tests must cover: no-argument full dump, single existing variable, multiple existing variables, missing variable (exit 1), mix of existing and missing variables, and -0 NUL-delimited output.\"\n48\t      - R3.3:\n49\t          text: Tests must verify that no error message is printed to stderr for missing variables.\n50\t\n51\tnon_goals:\n52\t  - cmd/printenv does not support setting or modifying variables; it is read-only.\n53\t  - cmd/printenv does not accept variable names from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n54\t  - cmd/printenv does not print the NAME= prefix when querying specific variables; only the value is printed.\n55\t\n56\tacceptance_criteria:\n57\t  - id: AC1\n58\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/printenv with no arguments produces the same output as gprintenv.\"\n59\t    traces:\n60\t      - R1.1\n61\t      - R1.2\n62\t      - R1.3\n63\t  - id: AC2\n64\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/printenv HOME produces the value of HOME followed by a newline, matching gprintenv HOME.\"\n65\t    traces:\n66\t      - R1.1\n67\t      - R1.2\n68\t      - R1.3\n69\t  - id: AC3\n70\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/printenv NONEXISTENT exits 1 with no output, matching gprintenv.\"\n71\t    traces:\n72\t      - R1.1\n73\t      - R2.2\n74\t      - R2.3\n75\t      - R2.4\n76\t      - R3.1\n77\t      - R3.2\n78\t  - id: AC4\n79\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/printenv -0 HOME terminates output with a NUL byte instead of a newline, matching gprintenv -0 HOME.\"\n80\t    traces:\n81\t      - R1.1\n82\t      - R1.2\n83\t      - R1.3\n84\t  - id: AC5\n85\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gprintenv passes for full dump, single variable, multiple variables, missing variables, and -0 mode.\"\n86\t    traces:\n87\t      - R3.1\n88\t  - id: AC6\n89\t    criterion: \"cmd/printenv compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n90\t    traces:\n91\t      - R1.1\n92\t      - R1.2\n93\t      - R1.3\n94\t      - R2.1\n95\t      - R2.2\n96\t      - R2.3\n97\t      - R2.4\n98\t      - R3.1\n99\t      - R3.2\n100\t      - R3.3\n101\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d79d2a8-8057-4438-ba57-a122ed62e4ca","uuid":"1a384674-ca87-402b-819b-129edd3133fd","timestamp":"2026-05-20T14:18:57.768Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5365/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd040-printenv.yaml","content":"id: srd040-printenv\ntitle: \"cmd/printenv: Print Environment Variables\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Scripts and debugging sessions need a simple way to inspect specific environment variables\n  or dump the entire environment. While env overlaps in functionality, printenv provides a\n  cleaner interface for querying named variables and reporting which ones are missing via its\n  exit code. The macOS BSD printenv lacks the -0 NUL-delimited flag available in GNU printenv.\n  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gprintenv, installed by\n  coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations and edge cases, verified by differential\n  testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print all environment variables when invoked with no arguments.\n  - G2: Print only the values of specified variables when one or more VARIABLE arguments are given.\n  - G3: Report success or failure via exit code depending on whether all requested variables exist.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print every environment variable on its own line in NAME=VALUE format and exit 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: When invoked with one or more VARIABLE arguments, must print only the value (not the name or '=') of each named variable, one per line, in the order given.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: If a named VARIABLE is not set in the environment, must produce no output for that variable and must not print an error message.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Output formatting and exit codes\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: -0 or --null must terminate each output line with a NUL byte (0x00) instead of a newline.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 0 if all requested VARIABLE arguments are found in the environment.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must exit 1 if any requested VARIABLE argument is not found in the environment.\n      - R2.4:\n          text: When no VARIABLE arguments are given, must always exit 0 (the dump of all variables cannot fail).\n\n  R3:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (gprintenv) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: no-argument full dump, single existing variable, multiple existing variables, missing variable (exit 1), mix of existing and missing variables, and -0 NUL-delimited output.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Tests must verify that no error message is printed to stderr for missing variables.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/printenv does not support setting or modifying variables; it is read-only.\n  - cmd/printenv does not accept variable names from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n  - cmd/printenv does not print the NAME= prefix when querying specific variables; only the value is printed.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/printenv with no arguments produces the same output as gprintenv.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/printenv HOME produces the value of HOME followed by a newline, matching gprintenv HOME.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/printenv NONEXISTENT exits 1 with no output, matching gprintenv.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/printenv -0 HOME terminates output with a NUL byte instead of a newline, matching gprintenv -0 HOME.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gprintenv passes for full dump, single variable, multiple variables, missing variables, and -0 mode.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/printenv compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":101,"startLine":1,"totalLines":101}}}
