{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler-scaffold orchestrator) requested implementation of task #5365: `[stitch] srd040-printenv R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1`. This is a code generation task to create the `printenv` utility in Go, which prints environment variables. The specific deliverables are:\n   - Create `cmd/printenv/main.go` - the printenv utility implementation\n   - Create `cmd/printenv/printenv_test.go` - differential tests against `gprintenv`\n   - Implement four specific requirements from srd040-printenv:\n     - R1.1: No args → print all env vars in NAME=VALUE format, exit 0\n     - R1.2: With VARIABLE args → print only values (not names), one per line, in order given\n     - R1.3: Missing VARIABLE → no output for that variable, no error message\n     - R2.1: `-0`/`--null` flag → terminate each output line with NUL byte (0x00) instead of newline\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU coreutils `printenv` utility\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against Homebrew GNU reference binary (`gprintenv`)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` and `pkg/testutils.BuildBinary` for test infrastructure\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gprintenv\")` with `t.Skip` for graceful degradation when reference binary unavailable\n   - NUL-delimited output mode (`-0`/`--null` flag)\n   - Exit code semantics: 0 if all vars found, 1 if any missing, always 0 for no-arg dump\n   - Copyright header required on all Go files\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n   - Build with `go build -o bin/printenv ./cmd/printenv/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd040-printenv.yaml` (READ)\n     - Full SRD defining printenv behavior, goals, requirements, non-goals, and acceptance criteria\n     - Key requirements: R1 (default behavior - R1.1, R1.2, R1.3), R2 (output formatting and exit codes - R2.1 through R2.4), R3 (differential testing - R3.1 through R3.3)\n     - Non-goals: no setting vars, no stdin input, no NAME= prefix when querying specific vars\n   \n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (provided in context)\n     - Contains `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` which must be called at start of main\n     ```go\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() {\n             <-c\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }()\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (provided in context)\n     - `DiffTest` struct: `{ Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles }`\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` runs all subtests\n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles the package and returns binary path\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/build.go` (provided in context)\n     - `BuildBinary(t, dir)` compiles Go package at dir, returns path to compiled binary\n\n   - `cmd/printenv/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - printenv utility with flag parsing for -0/--null\n     - Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` first\n\n   - `cmd/printenv/printenv_test.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests using testutils.RunDiffTests against gprintenv\n     - Must cover: no-arg full dump, single existing var, multiple vars, missing var (exit 1), mix of existing/missing, -0 NUL output\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only read the SRD file before being interrupted for summary.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the full specification before implementing\n   - No implementation work started yet\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: Massive task description with full project context, execution constitution, go style constitution, task requirements, constraints, design decisions, acceptance criteria, shared protocols, package contracts, and inline source code for all pkg/ packages. The task is to implement srd040-printenv R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Requesting a detailed summary of the conversation before continuing.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/printenv/main.go` implementing R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1\n   - Create `cmd/printenv/printenv_test.go` with differential tests against gprintenv\n   - Verify compilation: `go build -o bin/printenv ./cmd/printenv/`\n   - Verify vet: `go vet ./cmd/printenv/...`\n   - Run tests: `go test ./cmd/printenv/... -count=1`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd040-printenv.yaml` and was about to start implementing the two files. The implementation plan based on the SRD and all provided context:\n\n   **cmd/printenv/main.go** should:\n   - Start with copyright header\n   - Import `os`, `fmt`, `flag` (or manual arg parsing), and `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` first\n   - Parse `-0`/`--null` flag\n   - If no VARIABLE args: iterate `os.Environ()`, print each, terminate with NUL or newline based on flag, exit 0\n   - If VARIABLE args: for each, call `os.LookupEnv()`, print value if found (terminated by NUL or newline), track if any missing, exit 1 if any missing\n\n   **cmd/printenv/printenv_test.go** should:\n   - Use `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gprintenv\")`\n   - Skip if gprintenv not found\n   - Test cases: no-arg dump, single existing var (HOME), multiple vars, missing var (exit 1), mix of existing+missing, -0 NUL mode\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both `cmd/printenv/main.go` and `cmd/printenv/printenv_test.go` in full, then compile and test. Per the task instruction: \"Write all source files before runn